    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Zombieland (2009) revolutionized zombie comedy by injecting fresh humor into the undead genre. While <a href=\"/movie/747\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"747\">Shaun of the Dead</a> (2004) pioneered zombie comedy in the modern era, Zombieland's distinctly American take - complete with Twinkie quests and amusement park showdowns - created a new template for horror-comedy. The film's clever use of survival rules as both running gags and actual plot devices showed how to balance genuine zombie threats with laugh-out-loud moments. Bill Murray's legendary cameo remains one of cinema's greatest surprise appearances, perfectly capturing the film's blend of meta-humor and genuine heart."
      },
